[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m out-parameter and no sentinel. Every one of the 65 536 possible `uint16_t`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m values is a *valid* input that produces a defined result, so there is no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m "invalid input" for which C and Rust could disagree on a rejection.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
