[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     87[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Symptom.** `test_ffi_dirty_upper_bits` aborted the Rust `.so` with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     88[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `index out of bounds: the len is 2048 but the index is 29299`, SIGABRT (the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     89[0m:[38;5;10m[49m release profile sets `panic = "abort"`), where C returned a value.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     90[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     91[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Root cause**, from the disassembly of both sides:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     92[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     93[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - C narrows its own parameter. `gcc` emits `movzwl -0x14(%rbp),%eax` at the top
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     94[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   of `half2float`, so the callee reads only bits 0..15 of `%edi`. `n` is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     95[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   therefore always in `[0, 63]` no matter what the caller left in the register.
